<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gold Fields Namibia reports 3Q loss.</title>
<headline>Gold Fields Namibia reports 3Q loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-Sept versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million $Namibian unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss after tax	 25.17    vs   12.0 profit</p>
<p>    Capital spending	    5.75    vs    9.51</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled	    278,000    vs   374,000</p>
<p>Tonnes concentrates produced</p>
<p>    Copper			3,084     vs   5,990</p>
<p>    Lead			  1,068     vs   3,302</p>
<p>    Silver			    7     vs	12</p>
<p>Full name: Gold Fields Namibia Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the poor results were caused by a strike which began on August 22, low grades experienced at Kombat and the fall in the price of copper.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
